       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is well above the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day, and it's five times that ceiling. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity. Nothing in the patient's profile (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function) would justify it.\n\nMy guess is that it's a typo for **100 mg**, or possibly 50 mg, which is a common starting dose. Can you confirm the dose you want? Typical dosing is:\n\n- **Starting dose:** 25\u201350 mg PO once daily\n- **Usual range:** 50\u2013200 mg PO once daily\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg really is intended, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me and I'll note the clinical rationale on the order. I'd still recommend verifying it with pharmacy first."
      }
